From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: move wake-gpios to the Wi-Fi node

pci_configure_of_wake_gpio() reads the "wake" GPIO from the node of the
PCI device it is adding, then registers it as that device's wake IRQ.
Nothing reads wake-gpios from the pcie4 host bridge node, which the
binding deprecates anyway, so WAKE# from the Wi-Fi card has no handler
and can't take the system out of suspend.

Move the property to wifi@0, so the IRQ belongs to the device that drives
the line. The pin configuration stays in pcie4_default.

The ath11k PCI binding doesn't list wake-gpios yet and has
additionalProperties: false.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
index 691cbc7f2..bcf77a11b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -990,7 +990,6 @@ &pcie4 {
 	max-link-speed = <2>;
 
 	perst-gpios = <&tlmm 141 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 139 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 	vddpe-3v3-supply = <&vreg_wlan>;
 
@@ -1004,6 +1003,7 @@ &pcie4_port0 {
 	wifi@0 {
 		compatible = "pci17cb,1103";
 		reg = <0x10000 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
+		wake-gpios = <&tlmm 139 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 		vddrfacmn-supply = <&vreg_pmu_rfa_cmn_0p8>;
 		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_pmu_aon_0p8>;
